---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import portrait from '../../ashmit-profile.jpg';
---
<Layout>
  <div class="container">
    <header class="introduction">
      <div>
        <p class="affiliation">Computer Science · NYU Abu Dhabi</p>
        <h1>Ashmit Mukherjee</h1>
        <p>I’m a Computer Science senior with a minor in Economics. I’m interested in how people make decisions together, and how those decisions change when AI advice is involved.</p>
        <div class="intro-links"><a href="mailto:asm8879@nyu.edu">asm8879@nyu.edu</a><a href="https://github.com/Ansester" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub ↗</a></div>
      </div>
      <Image class="portrait" src={portrait} alt="Ashmit Mukherjee" width={144} height={144} format="webp" loading="eager" />
    </header>

    <section class="home-section" id="research" aria-labelledby="research-heading">
      <h2 id="research-heading">Research</h2>
      <article class="research-entry">
        <h3><a href="/work/human-ai-collaboration/">Human–AI collaboration</a></h3>
        <p class="byline">Research assistant with Ben Rosche and Hanan Salam · 2026–present</p>
        <p>I built the platform for experiments on AI advice and cooperation and lead its ongoing development, from the game rules and participant interfaces to the records used for analysis.</p>
        <p>I’m interested in what people learn from working with an assistant, and whether that carries over when the assistant is no longer there.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="research-entry" id="manuscript">
        <h3><a href="/work/protein-language-models/">Bio-LoRA and protein models</a></h3>
        <p class="byline">Research assistant, eBRAIN Lab · Co-first author, unpublished manuscript</p>
        <p>I built the signal-peptide evaluation for a study of adapting protein language models with biological information, and ran comparisons across three model sizes. Follow-up experiments examined which settings held up across repeated runs.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="research-entry">
        <h3><a href="/work/synthetic-pilot-lab/">Synthetic Pilot Lab</a></h3>
        <p class="byline">Independent capstone · 2026–present</p>
        <p>My capstone studies how to test experimental software before using it with participants. I built a benchmark that replays scripted decisions through correct and deliberately faulty game engines, with a separate evaluator to check the results. One test exposed incorrect individual payoffs that checks on the group total missed.</p>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section class="home-section" id="projects" aria-labelledby="projects-heading">
      <div class="section-heading"><h2 id="projects-heading">Other projects</h2><a href="/work/">All projects ↗</a></div>
      <p>I co-developed <a href="/work/roomwise/">RoomWise</a>, an app where you talk through what you want to buy, swipe through furniture listings, and see the room preview update with each selection. <a href="/work/fieldlens/">FieldLens</a> is a local-model tool for reading incident records and tracing answers back to their sources.</p>
      <p>I’ve also worked on <a href="/work/hinglish-ner/">Hindi–English named-entity recognition</a>, <a href="/work/salary-regression/">salary regression</a>, and <a href="/work/camp/">a campus equipment app</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="home-section" id="about" aria-labelledby="about-heading">
      <h2 id="about-heading">A little background</h2>
      <div id="background">
        <p>I expect to graduate in May 2027 and am preparing for doctoral research. Alongside human–AI interaction, I’m interested in applying computation to social, economic, and historical questions.</p>
        <p>I studied away at NYU Paris and NYU New York. At NYU Abu Dhabi, I’ve facilitated workshops for first-year students and worked front of house at the Arts Center.</p>
        <p id="experience">Previously, I was an <a href="/work/zeek/">ML engineering intern at Zeek</a>, working on customer segmentation and model comparison.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
